<title>UK: UK's TI up as Merrill upgrades to &quot;neutral&quot;.</title>
<headline>UK's TI up as Merrill upgrades to &quot;neutral&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in TI Group Plc rose on Monday as Merrill Lynch raised the stock to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;reduce&quot; after the engineering's group's 189 million stg bid for Sweden's Forsheda, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 3p at 559-1/2 by 1117 GMT, rebounding from last week's decline after Mannesmann AG sold its near nine percent stake in the company.</p>
<p>Sources said Merrill analysts highlighted the complementary nature of Forsheda's polymer business to its own operations in the field. The brokerage expects the acquisition to enhance TI's earnings by three percent next year, sources said.</p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
